                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer: I was provided a copy for my unbiased review.\n\n\nPlaying \"An Occasional Dream\" was like stepping back into time.  It brought me back to my younger years of JRPGs, when the voice acting wasn't something that could make or break a game and you could just enjoy the story.  This very much hit all the nostalgia buttons for me and I truly enjoyed playing this game.\n\nThe story and the characters felt pretty fleshed out.  I enjoyed the nod to the genre in the sense of the main character figuring out he is in an RPG by recognizing all the tropes (why are all the doors always unlocked and why does no one ever care when you bust in and take their stuff?  I have been wondering this for AGES).  I even liked the slight romantic element to the game, though I would have enjoyed maybe exploring that a little more.  I won't get into the ending (though I did like it and thought it was a little bittersweet) but I really would have liked to have some time to really get into the dynamic of the relationship.  \n\nThe battle system was well done as well.  It was easy enough to figure out and I liked the points to spend on abilities take for leveling.  The monsters looked great and I liked the added visuals for spell casting.  I was pretty happy to see that when I got the next level of the spell or ability that it was reflected in the game by the visuals.  \n\nThe map I thought was great and it reminded me of my old Secret of Mana feels.  My favorite area ended up being the snowy one.  The minimap is such a great tool as well and I was happy to see it on here.  \n\nWhen I play JRPGs I am one that really lives the grind it out part.  I spent a lot of time leveling and grinding up the characters.  This game definitely delivered when it comes to this and I am sure it is something I will do on my next play-through as well.\n\nI did dabble a bit in the end game content but I haven't gotten that far through it yet.  I did beat the main story and I look forward to seeing if there is a part 2 (I sure hope there is!).  Bottom line, this game is well worth the price and if you are a fan of the genre you shouldn't be disappointed.",
